From 02be7739db306897f2441562ee8d27dddc15d36c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:11:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: free the operator block's backing pointer array

adjust_order_ops_depth_block() freed the temporary operator tokens and
the operators struct, but not the separately allocated items backing
array, so every populated operator block of every parsed formula lost
that allocation - including the full formula parse at startup.  Free
the backing array along with the struct.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-formulas-calc.c b/src/borg/borg-formulas-calc.c
index ca7a0c261..f03aad371 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-formulas-calc.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-formulas-calc.c
@@ -431,6 +431,9 @@ static bool adjust_order_ops_depth_block(
         mem_free(operators->items[i]);
         operators->items[i] = NULL;
     }
+    /* Release the backing pointer array too: it is allocated separately
+     * by borg_array_add() once the block has an operator. */
+    mem_free(operators->items);
     mem_free(operators);
     operators = NULL;
 
